title: Wybory do Sejmu
new-page: true
call: polish_opening_state
on-arrival: {!
// The monthly router enters here after processing the month, before another
// ordinary action. Re-entry resumes the saved phase instead of creating a vote.
if (Q.polish_election_system && Q.sejm_election_due &&
        (!Q.sejm_pending || Q.sejm_pending.phase === 'complete')) {
    Q.sejm_pending = {
        id: 'sejm_' + Q.year + '_' + Q.month + '_' + (Q.n_elections + 1),
        year: Q.year, month: Q.month,
        first: !Q.sejm_first_election_completed, phase: 'pending'
    };
    Q.in_election = 1;
}
!}
go-to: results if sejm_forming_government; main if not sejm_election_in_progress

= Wybory do Sejmu — [+ month : month +] [+ year +]

[? if not sejm_first_election_completed : The Sejm election of 5 November 1922 is now due. Voting, results and government formation are compressed into one November sequence. A general Senate is not simulated; December will derive a proportional 111-seat snapshot only for the National Assembly. ChZJN contests as a joint ZLN–PSChD list. ?]

[? if sejm_first_election_completed : This is a continuation election using the shared 444-seat calculation. Its date and political context still come from the temporary legacy scheduler; later Polish chronology and alliances are not implemented. ?]

Campaigning and monthly effects determine voting intentions. We will record those votes once, allocate **444 MPs**, and then consider governments. A majority requires **223 MPs**. Reading these screens and choosing a government does not spend another monthly action.

- @calculate: Count the votes.

@calculate
go-to: election_algorithm
set-jump: sejm_election.allocate

@allocate
call: sejm_election_result
go-to: results if sejm_election_error = ""; error if sejm_election_error != ""

@error
new-page: true

= The election could not be calculated

[+ sejm_election_error +]

No parliamentary seats, election counter or history were changed. This indicates invalid simulation data, not an election outcome.

- @calculate: Retry the calculation.

@results
new-page: true
call: polish_opening_state
go-to: main if not sejm_has_result; government if sejm_has_result

= Sejm election result — [+ sejm_result_date +]

Each line separates **votes**, **MPs**, and **share of seats**. Changes refer to the previous parliament, not previous votes. Display rounding does not determine seats.

KPP: [+ kpp_election_display +]

PPS: [+ pps_election_display +]

NPR: [+ npr_election_display +]

PSL Wyzwolenie: [+ psl_wyzwolenie_election_display +]

PSL Piast: [+ psl_piast_election_display +]

[? if sejm_has_chzjn : ChZJN (ZLN + PSChD): [+ chzjn_election_display +] ?]

[? if not sejm_has_chzjn : PSChD: [+ pschd_election_display +] ?]

[? if not sejm_has_chzjn : ZLN: [+ zln_election_display +] ?]

Blok Mniejszości Narodowych: [+ minorities_bloc_election_display +]

Inne (separate small lists, not one alliance): [+ other_election_display +]

Total: [+ sejm_total_seats +] MPs. Majority: [+ sejm_majority_required +] MPs.

Largest electoral list(s): [+ sejm_largest_lists +]. Largest named parliamentary party/group(s): [+ sejm_largest_parties +].

[? if sejm_has_chzjn : ChZJN is displayed together, but ZLN and PSChD remain separate parties for relations and cabinet membership. Its MPs are attributed in proportion to their support at this election. ?]

[+ sejm_vote_comparison_notice +]

The Library's Figures and charts page shows the same parliament and recorded results. Later campaigning changes polling, not this election.

@government
call: polish_opening_state

= Government formation

PPS alone: [+ pps_seats +] MPs.

Koalicja Lewicy (PPS, Wyzwolenie, minority bloc): [+ polish_left_seats +] MPs.

Centre-left (PPS, Wyzwolenie, Piast, NPR): [+ polish_center_left_seats +] MPs.

PPS–Wyzwolenie cabinet: [+ pps_wyzwolenie_seats +] MPs; with external minority-bloc support: [+ polish_left_seats +] MPs.

Chjeno-Piast (ZLN, PSChD, Piast): [+ chjeno_piast_seats +] MPs.

Existing relationship requirements still apply. ChZJN is an electoral list, not an obligation to remain a parliamentary coalition. Named successor cabinets and ministry allocation remain unimplemented. The approved presidential succession follows in December without changing the selected government.

- @election_1928.polish_pps_majority: Form a PPS majority government.
- @election_1928.polish_left_coalition: Form Koalicja Lewicy.
- @election_1928.polish_center_left_coalition: Form a centre-left coalition.
- @election_1928.polish_minority_toleration: Form a PPS–Wyzwolenie government with external minority-bloc support.
- @election_1928.polish_chjeno_piast: Chjeno-Piast forms the government; PPS enters opposition.
- @election_1928.polish_opposition: Keep PPS in opposition.
- @return_to_play: Continue.

@return_to_play
view-if: not sejm_forming_government
go-to: root

@finish
call: polish_opening_state
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.sejm_pending && Q.sejm_pending.phase === 'results' && Q.sejm_pending.government_choice) {
    Q.sejm_pending.phase = 'complete';
    Q.in_election = 0;
}
!}

PPS position: [+ pps_government_position +].

This completes the election sequence without spending a monthly action. Parliamentary results remain fixed between elections. The approved presidential succession follows in December; government portfolios and subsequent historical cabinets still need their own Polish slice. Inherited Prussian executive powers remain unavailable. Generic welfare and wider monthly simulation are temporary legacy mechanics.

- @root: Resume play.
